Data in this folder

This folder is a sample of the data truffle.city runs on, enough to run the site locally. It is not licensed
under the FSL-1.1-MIT that covers the code. Each part keeps the terms of its source.

OpenStreetMap

tiles/basemap.pmtiles (roads, water, town names and named places), places.json (town and neighborhood
names), and the place names and kinds on lots in snapshot.json.gz and tiles/lots.pmtiles are derived from
OpenStreetMap data.

  © OpenStreetMap contributors. https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

That data is available under the Open Data Commons Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0:
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/
If you publicly use a database derived from it, you must also offer that database under the ODbL, and you
must keep the attribution above wherever the data or a map made from it is shown.

Public records

The lots in snapshot.json.gz, tiles/lots.pmtiles and daily.json (parcel numbers, outlines, addresses, land
and building values, land use, year added, neighborhood) and their zoning come from public records:

- Palm Beach County property records (Palm Beach County Property Appraiser parcel data)
- City of Boca Raton zoning districts
- Palm Beach County zoning (unincorporated land)
- Outside Palm Beach County the live site reads the Florida Department of Revenue statewide cadastral
  data; none of it is in this sample.

The values are the county's assessed values as published, not appraisals, and say nothing about what a lot
would sell for. Check each source's own terms before you reuse its records.

What the sample holds

Only lots that are not homes: businesses, civic and public land, and other non-residential land in
Downtown Boca Raton and West Boca (497 records). Houses, condominiums, townhouses, manufactured homes and
land the county lists as empty residential land are left out of the records and the tiles, so this
repository carries no list of home addresses or home values.
